 "_about": "The words the game composes from a piece's numbers (Ryan, 20 November: \"That's literally the gameplay explanation of how the weapon works. I need to be able to change it, and how would it ever get localized?\"): every line of a component's die readout and codex row, its compact line, a machine's lines on the die's hold, and a foe move's lines, as templates sim/templates.gd fills. text is the template, a brace a value the game fills in; fills is what the code that prints it fills, so a brace outside it fails the build; a text written as forms ({\"one\": ..., \"other\": ...}) picks its form by the count named in count (English: one for 1, other for any other). A rule line is written lower case, as the compact line runs it on, and the readout capitalises its first letter. A name inside a line (a term's, a component's, a move's) is its entry's own, never written here. Shown text: Ryan's to write, on the hangar's Text tab, its slots in tools/hangar_text.py.",
